g."]}, "overview": "Vicente Gonzalez seeks another term in a South Texas district that leans slightly Republican on paper but that he has held through competitive cycles. Eric Flores has raised substantial money, yet Gonzalez holds a cash advantage and both sides face heavy outside opposition spending. A late October Washington Post/Schar poll showed Gonzalez ahead 50-43 among likely voters, consistent with earlier narrower surveys.\n\nMost expert raters place the race at Lean D, with a couple of Likely D ratings and one Tossup call. Prediction markets price a Gonzalez win as near-certain, which looks stronger than the polling and district fundamentals warrant. The forecast expects Gonzalez to win by a moderate margin, with real but limited downside risk.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7969, "margin": 4.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7826, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7895, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8125, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7373, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7369, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7694, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7446, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8106, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7774, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7834, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7562, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7186, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7472, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7411, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7622, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7079, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7312, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.7593, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7567, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.7577, "ma